The IsEnabledAsync method in RequirePermissionsSimpleStateChecker calls context.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<IPermissionChecker>(), so I want to test that it correctly calls IsGrantedAsync on the IPermissionChecker mock and returns the expected results.

I will create a test class for RequirePermissionsSimpleStateChecker<TState> with a mock IPermissionChecker injected via a mocked IServiceProvider in the SimpleStateCheckerContext<TState>. I will test the cases of one permission and multiple permissions with RequiresAll true and false.

I will apply the make_virtual refactor to IsEnabledAsync to allow overriding in a test subclass if needed, but here it is an instance method so it should be fine to test as is.

I will submit the test now. It will use Moq for mocking and xUnit for testing.

